knowledge:
- key_parameters:
    - alias = Name used to label the cell population; must form a uniquely identifiable path with its parent nodes ;;
    - pop = Population patterns (e.g., "+", "-", "+/-", "++", "+/-+/-", "*") specifying which side of a 1-D gate or quadrant of a 2-D gate to keep ;;
    - parent = The parent population alias, which must be uniquely identifiable ;;
    - dims = Comma-separated character string specifying the dimensions (channels or markers) used for gating ;;
    - gating_method = The name of the gating function (e.g., "mindensity", "singletGate", "flowClust", "tailgate", "quantileGate", "boundary", "quadGate.tmix") ;;
    - gating_args = Named arguments passed directly to the underlying gating function (e.g., "gate_range=c(1,3)", "K=2", "target=c(1e5,5e4)", "tol=0.05", "probs=0.99") ;;
    - collapseDataForGating = Logical (TRUE/FALSE); when TRUE, samples are collapsed before gating and the gate is replicated across all samples ;;
    - groupBy = Variable or numeric value used to group samples before preprocessing or gating ;;
    - preprocessing_method = Name of the preprocessing function (e.g., "prior_flowClust", "standardize_flowset") used to generate prior information for gating
- alternatives:
    - Manual gating in FlowJo = Traditional manual gating, which can be imported into R using CytoML (e.g., open_flowjo_xml and flowjo_to_gatingset) but is subjective and slow for large datasets ;;
    - Interactive gating = Prototyping gates directly on a GatingSet using gs_add_gating_method and gs_remove_gating_method without a CSV template
- when_to_use: Use when analyzing large-scale, high-throughput flow cytometry, CyTOF, or cross-laboratory datasets where manual gating is too time-consuming, subjective, and non-reproducible.
- pitfalls:
    - mindensity failure = If there are more than 2 major peaks, mindensity may cut between the wrong peaks. Use gate_range, min, or max in gating_args to restrict the search space, or adjust the smoothing factor (adjust) ;;
    - Single peak gating = mindensity will fail if only one major peak is detected. Use tailgate (gate_tail) or quantileGate instead ;;
    - Rare populations = Standard density-based gating may miss rare populations. Use quantileGate with high probs (e.g., 0.99) to capture them ;;
    - 2D gating dimension order = The order of dimensions in dims (x-axis first, y-axis second) determines how gates are displayed, though it does not affect the gating process itself
